        "tree_id": "86d83880204979396261a18c08c3bfeb246b5dcf",
        "message": "fix(M7): canonical tool-state consistency + strict tool args + model identity audit\n\nCloses the L1 semantic defect (Coder Directions §2): getFinancials\nfetched live fundamentals before resolving metrics, but getStock/\ngetScore/getPeers called resolveStockMetrics(symbol) with no live\noverlay — two tools in one AI loop could answer from different data\nstates for the same symbol (package + getFinancials live-capable;\ngetScore/getStock seed baseline).\n\nFix — one canonical observation state per request (no duplicated\nscoring logic; the tools REUSE the canonical resolver/builders):\n- lib/ai/evidence.ts: createCanonicalStockState() — per-symbol\n  memoized bounded fundamentals fetch + price observation + resolver\n  application. The price promise is memoized RAW: the package catches\n  a throwing surface (honest unavailable item) while getPrices\n  propagates it (explicit failed state) — one observation, two\n  consumption contracts\n- lib/ai/tools.ts: every tool resolves through the shared state;\n  executeAiTool(call, deps, state) threads it (fresh state from deps\n  when omitted — single-call callers unchanged)\n- lib/ai/router.ts: GenerateArgs.stockState; the loop passes it through\n- app/api/chat: ONE state per request, shared by buildAiEvidencePackage\n  AND the tool loop — the initial evidence score and getScore's score\n  fact are byte-identical (id + typed facts + text) for the same symbol\n  in the same request\n\nStrict tool arguments (§3): SymbolArgsSchema/PeersArgsSchema are now\nzod .strict() — an unexpected argument is an invalid-args FAILURE,\nnever a silently stripped key (a forged result member or smuggled\ninstruction cannot ride the args).\n\nFail-first evidence (Rule 21): test/aiToolState.test.ts — 7 failing on\nthe pre-M7 tree (state consistency ×4 incl. byte-identical score\nitems; strict args ×2; forged-result ×1), all green now. The matrix\nalso pins: wrong type/missing/oversized symbol, case normalization,\nunknown symbol/tool, a forged TOOL RESULT as model text (G4 honest\nstate, forged numbers never displayed).\n\nModel identity (§4): scripts/auditModelIdentity.ts + evidence\ndocs/evidence/commit-m/model-identity-audit.json —\nDEFAULT_OPENAI_MODEL 'agnes-2.5-flash' is INDEPENDENTLY ESTABLISHED:\nproduction env sets CHAT_MODEL=agnes-2.5-flash on\nhttps://apihub.agnes-ai.com/v1 (registry-APPROVED), the provider's own\n/models list contains the id, and completions echo\nmodel=agnes-2.5-flash. Registry honesty fixes: the CHAT_API entry now\nnames the ACTUAL provider (agnes-ai.com, not openai.com — the endpoint\nis an OpenAI-compatible aggregator; FD-8 terms review stays OPEN);\n/rishis no longer hardcodes a 'Google Gemini 2.5 Flash' fallback label\n(it says 'model: not yet reported' until provenance supplies one).\n\nEval harness determinism: router cases thread an offline stock state\n(scripted fetch replaces globalThis.fetch, so the state's default live\nsurfaces must not run); cases keep their explicit fixtures.\n\nGates: tsc --noEmit 0; vitest 706/706; eval:chat 113/113 (102 local +\n11 CI-delegated); freeAccessAudit PASS.",
